            <ArticleTitle>Complications associated with combined use of abciximab and an intracoronary thrombolytic agent (urokinase or tissue-type plasminogen activator).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>518-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A potent platelet inhibitor combined with an intracoronary thrombolytic agent is aggressive therapy that may be used for high-risk, complex, refractory thrombotic coronary lesions. A retrospective review of the records of 56 patients who received abciximab plus an intracoronary thrombolytic agent during a coronary interventional procedure did not reveal a prohibitive incidence of major bleeding with this combination therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
